   "accessed": "2026-11-22",
   "note": "Outlines read off the three views (tools/trace/cn35/); only measurements are taken, not the drawing. The manufacturer's own dimensioned three-view of the CN-235-300, a brochure illustration (embedded pictures at about 27.8 px a meter), not an airport-planning sheet (none is public). The pages carry EADS-CASA's proprietary-information notice; the document has been public on nifc.gov since 2002. Scaled by its printed 21.40 m overall length; span within 0.4% of the printed 25.81 m; the plan drawn 1.3% long lengthwise, evened out. It draws its tailplane 9.4% wider than its printed 10.20 m (narrowed to it), its propellers 0.3 m further apart in the front view than the printed 7.0 m (placed by it) and smaller than the text's 3.66 m (given), and labels a wheelbase it draws 17% longer (6.20 m printed, 7.25 m drawn; the USACE gives 6.92 m). Main gear sponsons left out. Confidence medium."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://transportation.erdc.dren.mil/tsmcx/downloads/Military%20Aircraft%20Characteristics%20TSC%2013-2%20Dec%2013%20Rev%202.pdf",
